WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.775
Try it.

2
00:00:00.775 --> 00:00:06.025
Lab 1 runs in the provider notices
folder of the examples, in PowerShell 7.

3
00:00:06.025 --> 00:00:10.702
The account is AWS's documentation
account, one one one one two

4
00:00:10.702 --> 00:00:15.562
two two two three three three
three, in the commercial partition.

5
00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:17.950
Nothing signs in or sends a request.

6
00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:20.525
Step one lists what AWS needs.

7
00:00:20.525 --> 00:00:26.287
Three calls: describe events, describe event
details and describe affected entities,

8
00:00:26.287 --> 00:00:31.400
each with its one read action, and each
verified against AWS's documentation.

9
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.712
Three read actions, one per call.

10
00:00:33.712 --> 00:00:35.975
That's the whole policy,
and it's what you'd

11
00:00:35.975 --> 00:00:38.650
show an assessor who asks
what the reader may do.

12
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:42.100
Step two shows each partition's
Health endpoint region.

13
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.446
The commercial partition
reads from u s east one,

14
00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.488
with A R Ns that start A R N colon A W S.

15
00:00:49.488 --> 00:00:53.993
The GovCloud partition
reads from u s gov west one,

16
00:00:53.993 --> 00:00:58.560
with A R Ns that start A R N
colon A W S dash U S dash gov.
